portfolio_note:
The 13 candidates come from 8 mechanism classes, so the legs are not one bet:
- overnight-bias ORB (onr_orb on NQ, ES, GC);
- 15:00 late-day momentum (new day_move block on NQ and ES);
- quiet-day stop-run fade at levels (sweep_rev plus a new quiet day rule);
- two-anchor VWAP pullback limit (avwap_touch 15m);
- volume breakout (rvol_break on ES 15m, GC 15m and NQ 30m);
- open-side FVG pullback (ES 30m);
- VWAP-side opening-range break, long only (ES 15m);
- GC VWAP pullback (jj_fair 15m).

Trades: each leg makes about 0.35-1.0 a day. If all 13 passed that is about 8 a day. At past pass rates expect 0-3 legs, so the portfolio still needs more batches.

Lowest correlation with the morning NQ breakout cluster: day_move (a different clock, 15:00-15:58), sweep_q (a fade), touch_gx_15, and the GC legs.

Seen (earlier reads overlap this hunt's test months): nq_onrorb_15 (its 10:00 reading was read unseen 2025-07..2026-10), nq_daymove_15, nq_sweepq_5 (the pd value).

Two pieces of new code are needed:
1. The `day_move` family.
2. The `quiet`/`busy` day rules. hmread's C3 should then draw its random entries on the same quiet days.

No-code fallbacks:
- for day_move: noise_band pm 15m with w_start 14:55 / w_end 15:05, as a long card and a short card;
- for the sweep: drop days quiet. Expect about break-even then.

Plumbing to check before running:
(1) onr_orb flattens at 15:30 and stretches one nyam pass, but the random pool holds to 15:58. Its old code check failed on trades outside the window: re-run check_spec first.
(2) The vwap_dev gate resets at every pass, so in mid and pm it is an 11:00 / 13:30 VWAP. This affects sweepq and es_orbcl.
(3) NQ 30m has no c1f random pool yet; the first run builds it.
(4) Idea 19 (GC 03:00 candle, tod_drift us_short / eve_long, Asia break) and idea 20 (holy grail, volspike pm) have pre-registered specs but no store in runs_wf. Idea 18's stores are missing from is_hm.csv / SELECTION_HM.md. Running them costs no new registration.

Left out on purpose:
- both-sided GC release brackets (banned);
- the 03:00 London candle (its edge needed 3R; hm60 caps targets at 2R; night is dead in-sample);
- the ES/NQ rv z-exit (an exit outside hm60);
- the 09:30 30-minute candle (its entries already failed an unseen read);
- big_print and ddiv (no direction on build days);
- Level-2 and filter blocks (refused on the 3:1 route).

Honest prior: the in-sample median box sits 1-5 points under the bar. Prior build-day evidence says trend rules are weakest in Jan/May/Sep, so the breakout-class candidates here (rvol_break, orbcl, onr_orb) carry that risk.
